result.prior_funding_conflicts:
EXCLUDES (verbatim): "Not previously a recipient of an ASM Microbe travel award within the last 2 years."

The critical, non-obvious reading: the bar is the whole ASM Microbe travel-award FAMILY, not this award alone. I verified the identical sentence on the sibling pages — the Richard and Mary Finkelstein Student Travel Award and the Clinical Virology Travel Awards both carry "Not previously a recipient of an ASM Microbe travel award within the last 2 years." So winning ANY ASM Microbe travel award (Finkelstein, Clinical Virology, Carlyn Halde, Fellows, etc.) starts a 2-year clock that blocks this one, and vice versa. Applicants who think of these as separate competitions get this wrong.

PRESERVES ELIGIBILITY — with an important caveat about the evidence type. ASM states exactly ONE prior-award bar, the 2-year one above. Nothing on the page restricts applicants who hold or have held:
- federal research funding (NIH, NSF) or fellowship support — no exclusion stated;
- institutional or departmental travel funds — no exclusion stated;
- travel awards from other societies or from ASM meetings other than ASM Microbe — no exclusion stated;
- an ASM Microbe travel award received MORE than 2 years ago — the bar is explicitly time-limited, so it lapses rather than being permanent.
Also preserving: the mechanism is open across three career stages at once ("An undergraduate student, graduate student or postdoctoral researcher"), and there is no citizenship or nationality restriction; ASM membership, not nationality, is the gate.

HONESTY FLAG on the preserving half: these are ABSENCES of a stated exclusion, not explicit written carve-outs. ASM publishes no "does not affect eligibility" language of the kind NIH uses for the R01/K interaction. I did not find, and am not asserting, an affirmative ASM statement permitting concurrent federal funding — only that no such bar is published. Anyone relying on it for a borderline case should confirm with ASM.

UNVERIFIED, and worth asking about: whether you may apply to two ASM Microbe travel awards in the SAME cycle (the 2-year bar speaks to having "previously" received one, not to concurrent applications). Separate solicitation IDs make concurrent application mechanically possible; no page permits or forbids it.

result.loi_deadline:
n/a — there is no letter of intent or pre-proposal stage.

But there IS a hard upstream gate that functions like one and must be cleared weeks before 15 July, because the student CANNOT SELF-APPLY. This is a nomination award. Before a package can exist:
(a) IEEE EDS *student membership* must already be active — required "at the time of nomination", not at award;
(b) an IEEE EDS-member nominator/sponsor must agree to write the nominating letter. The 2026 flyer adds that the nominator should "preferable be serving as the candidate's faculty advisor";
(c) TWO further recommendation letters must come from people who are NOT the nominator.

Practical effect: the real deadline for a candidate is whenever their advisor must be approached, plus EDS membership enrolment time — not 15 July.
